window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-099.json",{"day":99,"title":"A Coastal Reserve Beyond the Postcard","targetWords":[{"word":"pollute","gloss":"污染","context":"Few expected to spend their first hour learning why a town should not pollute the water flowing through its canal.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"hemisphere","gloss":"半球","context":"A display near a cave compared wildlife in each hemisphere.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"bush","gloss":"灌木","context":"A bush cast shade over the field, while a fallen leaf returned nutrients to the soil.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"pyramid","gloss":"金字塔","context":"Before leaving, the group studied a pyramid-shaped diagram of feeding relationships.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"lightning","gloss":"闪电","context":"Above them, a storm cloud darkened the summit and lightning briefly lit the hillside.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"shadow","gloss":"阴影","context":"They waited under shelter as a sharp shadow disappeared from the lawn.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"rainbow","gloss":"彩虹","context":"Visitors usually arrived at the coastal reserve hoping to see a whale or photograph a rainbow above the bay.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"shell","gloss":"外壳","context":"A plastic shell of packaging on the sand could remain long after the holidaymaker who dropped it had returned home.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"volcano","gloss":"火山","context":"A distant volcano released steam, reminding visitors that not all environmental change came from human activity.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"whale","gloss":"鲸","context":"Visitors usually arrived at the coastal reserve hoping to see a whale or photograph a rainbow above the bay.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"fertile","gloss":"肥沃的","context":"Beyond the entrance, a herd of cattle grazed near a fertile acre of farmland.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"herd","gloss":"畜群","context":"Beyond the entrance, a herd of cattle grazed near a fertile acre of farmland.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"steam","gloss":"蒸汽","context":"A distant volcano released steam, reminding visitors that not all environmental change came from human activity.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"wet","gloss":"潮湿的","context":"The guide began beside a wet patch of dirt and mud where a worm, an ant, and a spider were easy to find.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"exotic","gloss":"外来的","context":"Children examined an exotic snake behind protective glass and watched a bubble rise in a tank that demonstrated water circulation.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"leaf","gloss":"叶子","context":"A bush cast shade over the field, while a fallen leaf returned nutrients to the soil.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"bay","gloss":"海湾","context":"Visitors usually arrived at the coastal reserve hoping to see a whale or photograph a rainbow above the bay.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"hurricane","gloss":"飓风","context":"From this height, the guide described a hurricane that had changed the coastline and a shower that had washed litter into the bay only the previous week.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"shore","gloss":"海岸","context":"These small organisms supported relationships that continued far beyond the shore.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"tide","gloss":"潮水","context":"A small flock circled above the tide.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"wing","gloss":"翅膀","context":"The path climbed toward a cliff, where a pigeon rested in a nest and another bird stretched its wing.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"cattle","gloss":"牛","context":"Beyond the entrance, a herd of cattle grazed near a fertile acre of farmland.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"litter","gloss":"垃圾","context":"From this height, the guide described a hurricane that had changed the coastline and a shower that had washed litter into the bay only the previous week.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"ant","gloss":"蚂蚁","context":"The guide began beside a wet patch of dirt and mud where a worm, an ant, and a spider were easy to find.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"bubble","gloss":"气泡","context":"Children examined an exotic snake behind protective glass and watched a bubble rise in a tank that demonstrated water circulation.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"cliff","gloss":"悬崖","context":"The path climbed toward a cliff, where a pigeon rested in a nest and another bird stretched its wing.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"pigeon","gloss":"鸽子","context":"The path climbed toward a cliff, where a pigeon rested in a nest and another bird stretched its wing.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"shade","gloss":"阴凉","context":"A bush cast shade over the field, while a fallen leaf returned nutrients to the soil.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"canal","gloss":"运河","context":"Few expected to spend their first hour learning why a town should not pollute the water flowing through its canal.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"log","gloss":"木头","context":"A pig rooted beside an old log, and a duck led its young away from a shallow pit.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"shower","gloss":"阵雨","context":"From this height, the guide described a hurricane that had changed the coastline and a shower that had washed litter into the bay only the previous week.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"worm","gloss":"蚯蚓","context":"The guide began beside a wet patch of dirt and mud where a worm, an ant, and a spider were easy to find.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"duck","gloss":"鸭","context":"A pig rooted beside an old log, and a duck led its young away from a shallow pit.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"lawn","gloss":"草坪","context":"They waited under shelter as a sharp shadow disappeared from the lawn.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"nest","gloss":"窝","context":"The path climbed toward a cliff, where a pigeon rested in a nest and another bird stretched its wing.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"predator","gloss":"捕食者","context":"In fact, a simplified landscape could become less resilient when one disease or predator disturbed its remaining balance.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"spider","gloss":"蜘蛛","context":"The guide began beside a wet patch of dirt and mud where a worm, an ant, and a spider were easy to find.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"summit","gloss":"山顶","context":"Above them, a storm cloud darkened the summit and lightning briefly lit the hillside.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"acre","gloss":"英亩","context":"Beyond the entrance, a herd of cattle grazed near a fertile acre of farmland.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"bee","gloss":"蜜蜂","context":"Farmers had once treated every unfamiliar insect as a pest, but an ecologist showed how a bee helped crops reproduce.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"cave","gloss":"洞穴","context":"A display near a cave compared wildlife in each hemisphere.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"dirt","gloss":"泥土","context":"The guide began beside a wet patch of dirt and mud where a worm, an ant, and a spider were easy to find.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"pig","gloss":"猪","context":"A pig rooted beside an old log, and a duck led its young away from a shallow pit.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"pit","gloss":"坑","context":"A pig rooted beside an old log, and a duck led its young away from a shallow pit.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"zoo","gloss":"动物园","context":"An elephant photographed in another reserve appeared beside images from a zoo, prompting discussion of conservation and captivity.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"elephant","gloss":"大象","context":"An elephant photographed in another reserve appeared beside images from a zoo, prompting discussion of conservation and captivity.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"flock","gloss":"鸟群","context":"A small flock circled above the tide.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"mud","gloss":"泥","context":"The guide began beside a wet patch of dirt and mud where a worm, an ant, and a spider were easy to find.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"pest","gloss":"害虫","context":"Farmers had once treated every unfamiliar insect as a pest, but an ecologist showed how a bee helped crops reproduce.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"snake","gloss":"蛇","context":"Children examined an exotic snake behind protective glass and watched a bubble rise in a tank that demonstrated water circulation.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"Visitors usually arrived at the coastal reserve hoping to see a whale or photograph a rainbow above the bay. Few expected to spend their first hour learning why a town should not pollute the water flowing through its canal. The guide began beside a wet patch of dirt and mud where a worm, an ant, and a spider were easy to find. These small organisms supported relationships that continued far beyond the shore. The reserve was not merely a collection of impressive animals. It was a system whose health depended on ordinary decisions about farming, drainage, tourism, and waste.","zh":"游客来到海岸保护区，通常希望看鲸鱼，或拍摄海湾上方的彩虹。很少有人料到，第一小时会学习城镇为什么不该污染流经运河的水。向导从一片混着湿泥的土地开始，那里容易找到蚯蚓、蚂蚁和蜘蛛。这些小生物支持的关系延伸到海岸之外。保护区不只是令人惊叹的动物集合，而是健康程度取决于农业、排水、旅游与垃圾等日常决策的系统。"},{"en":"Beyond the entrance, a herd of cattle grazed near a fertile acre of farmland. A pig rooted beside an old log, and a duck led its young away from a shallow pit. Farmers had once treated every unfamiliar insect as a pest, but an ecologist showed how a bee helped crops reproduce. A bush cast shade over the field, while a fallen leaf returned nutrients to the soil. Making the land productive did not require removing every wild feature. In fact, a simplified landscape could become less resilient when one disease or predator disturbed its remaining balance.","zh":"入口之外，一群牛在肥沃的一英亩农田附近吃草。猪在旧木头旁拱土，鸭子带着幼崽离开浅坑。农民过去把每种陌生昆虫都当成害虫，但生态学家说明蜜蜂怎样帮助作物繁殖。灌木为田地遮阴，落叶把养分还给土壤。提高土地生产力并不要求清除每种野生元素。实际上，一旦疾病或捕食者扰乱所剩平衡，过度简化的景观可能更加脆弱。"},{"en":"The path climbed toward a cliff, where a pigeon rested in a nest and another bird stretched its wing. A small flock circled above the tide. From this height, the guide described a hurricane that had changed the coastline and a shower that had washed litter into the bay only the previous week. A distant volcano released steam, reminding visitors that not all environmental change came from human activity. Nevertheless, natural forces were no excuse for preventable damage. A plastic shell of packaging on the sand could remain long after the holidaymaker who dropped it had returned home.","zh":"小路向悬崖攀升，鸽子停在巢中，另一只鸟伸展翅膀，一小群鸟在潮水上盘旋。向导从高处讲述曾改变海岸线的飓风，以及上周把垃圾冲进海湾的阵雨。远处火山释放蒸汽，提醒游客并非所有环境变化都来自人类。然而，自然力量不能成为可避免破坏的借口。沙上的塑料包装外壳可能在丢弃它的游客回家很久之后，依然留在那里。"},{"en":"A display near a cave compared wildlife in each hemisphere. An elephant photographed in another reserve appeared beside images from a zoo, prompting discussion of conservation and captivity. Children examined an exotic snake behind protective glass and watched a bubble rise in a tank that demonstrated water circulation. Above them, a storm cloud darkened the summit and lightning briefly lit the hillside. They waited under shelter as a sharp shadow disappeared from the lawn. The interruption made a useful lesson concrete: a landscape is active and unpredictable, rather than a permanent background arranged for human enjoyment.","zh":"洞穴附近的展板比较两个半球的野生动物。另一保护区拍摄的大象与动物园照片并列，引出保护与圈养的讨论。孩子隔着防护玻璃观察外来蛇类，并看演示水循环的水箱中升起气泡。头顶暴风云遮暗山顶，闪电短暂照亮山坡。他们在遮蔽处等待，看草坪上清晰的影子消失。这次中断让一个教训具体可见：景观是活动而不可预测的，并非为人类享乐布置的永久背景。"},{"en":"Before leaving, the group studied a pyramid-shaped diagram of feeding relationships. Its broad foundation contained organisms that rarely appeared in tourist brochures, while its narrow top depended on everything beneath it. The guide asked visitors to consider which part their own choices affected. Buying food from a responsible farm, avoiding unnecessary packaging, and keeping to marked paths were modest actions, but they had identifiable consequences. The reserve offered wonder without pretending that wonder alone would protect it. People were more likely to care for the coast when they understood not only what lived there, but how their lives were connected to it.","zh":"离开前，团队研究金字塔形的食物关系图。宽阔底层包含很少出现在旅游宣传册里的生物，狭窄顶层则依靠下方一切。向导请游客思考自身选择影响哪个部分。从负责任的农场购买食物、避免多余包装、沿标记路线行走，都是小行动，却有可以识别的结果。保护区带来惊奇，却不假装只有惊奇就能保护它。人们理解海岸不仅住着什么，还理解自身生活如何与之相连时，才更可能珍惜它。"}],"previous":98,"next":100});
